Sections 3.2 to 3.12 give each function its trigger, actors, screens, processing, rules and abnormal cases. *Tests* names the automated test cases of Report 5 that check the function (catalogue `docs/backend/04_Test_Catalog.md`); BR-nn refers to the business rules of section 5.1, MSG to the messages of section 5.3. Error answers use the API's error format: an HTTP status, a stable code and a message in the user's language.

### 3.2 Accounts and access (AUTH)

#### 3.2.1 FR-AUTH-01 Sign in with a password

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | The user opens the web app or the Android app without a session, or the session ended. |
| Actors | Student, Staff, Manager, Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-01 Sign In (`/signin`); Android sign-in |
| Description | The user enters email and password and may tick *Remember me*. The API checks the BCrypt hash and returns a session token (random, stored hashed) with the user's role, Blocks and language; the app opens the role's home. |
| Rules and validation | Email and password required (field messages). Wrong password and unknown email get the same answer. Five wrong passwords in a row lock the account for the configured minutes, even for the right password then. A disabled, locked or rejected account cannot sign in; a rejected student sees the Manager's reason. Sign-out revokes the token at once. |
| Abnormal cases | 401 invalid credentials; 423 account locked (time left shown); 403 when a role calls another role's endpoint. |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-001, 002, 003, 004, 005, 006, 041 |

#### 3.2.2 FR-AUTH-02 Sign in with an FPT Google account

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | *Sign in with Google* on the sign-in page. |
| Actors | Student, back-office users with a linked Google account |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-01 Sign In; SCR-AUTH-05 Set a password |
| Description | The Google popup (or redirect when popups are blocked) returns a code or an ID token; the API verifies it with Google and requires the `fpt.edu.vn` hosted domain. An existing account signs in. An unknown FPT student address creates a student account without a password; until a password is set every page leads to *Set a password*. An address whose student code matches an imported, unused account signs in to that account (Verified). |
| Rules and validation | Exactly one of code and credential; the redirect flow only for the web app's own sign-in page. |
| Abnormal cases | 401 used or expired code (retry); 503 `GOOGLE_SIGN_IN_DISABLED` when Google is not configured or cannot be reached; a non-FPT address is refused. |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-009, 010, 029–033, 038, 040, 051, 052 |

#### 3.2.3 FR-AUTH-03 Passwords: forgot, reset, invitation and change

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | *Forgot password* link; an invitation email; Account › Change password. |
| Actors | All |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-02 Forgot password, SCR-AUTH-03 Reset password, SCR-AUTH-04 Set password (invitation), SCR-AUTH-05 Set a password |
| Description | Forgot password sends a one-use reset link by email (the answer never says whether the email exists). The link or an invitation link sets a new password; a reset signs out every earlier session. Change password needs the current one and keeps the current session. |
| Rules and validation | Password policy (length and character classes) checked on the server; a link works once and expires. |
| Abnormal cases | Weak password: field message, the link stays usable; used or expired link; wrong current password: field error, nothing changed. |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-007, 012, 022–027 |

#### 3.2.4 FR-AUTH-04 Student account verification

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | A new Google account without a match in the student list; the Manager's verification list. |
| Actors | Student, Manager |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-06 Account verification (sign-up form); SCR-AUTH-13 Students (filter *Waiting for verification*); SCR-AUTH-14 Student hub |
| Description | The student sends a form: student code, full name, gender, date of birth, major, cohort, phone. The account becomes *Pending verification*: it can read everything but cannot apply. A Manager verifies it (fields locked afterwards) or rejects it with a reason (account locked, student signed out). A later import that matches verifies it automatically. |
| Rules and validation | Every field checked; the student code format and uniqueness (BR-35); a pending account cannot apply (BR-02). |
| Abnormal cases | Code already used by another account; rejected account at sign-in shows the reason. |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-039, 042, 044, 045, TC-APP-022 |

#### 3.2.5 FR-AUTH-05 Import the student list

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Residents › Import student list. |
| Actors | Manager, Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-15 Import student list |
| Description | Download the template, upload CSV (UTF-8; comma, semicolon or tab) or XLSX, preview each line as New, Update, Unchanged or Error with the reason, then confirm. Confirming creates or updates the directory records, verifies waiting accounts that match and writes the import to the Audit Log. |
| Rules and validation | Matched on the student code; columns: code, full name, email, gender, date of birth, major, cohort, semester, hometown, region, enrollment status, priority groups; an email used by another account is an error; nothing is saved while errors remain. |
| Abnormal cases | Unknown or missing columns; a file without data; dates as text or Excel day numbers both accepted. |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-046, 047, 048 |

#### 3.2.6 FR-AUTH-06 Back-office users, roles and permissions

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › System › Users and Roles. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-11 Users and Roles |
| Description | Lists back-office accounts with role and Blocks; invites a user (email with a set-password link), changes role and Blocks, disables or restores an account (disabling signs the user out at once), shows the permission matrix that the API enforces. |
| Rules and validation | Invitation fields named per field; the Admin cannot disable themselves; every change is audited. |
| Abnormal cases | Duplicate email; Staff or Manager opening Admin screens get 403. |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-011, 013–017 |

#### 3.2.7 FR-AUTH-07 Staff accounts and workload

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Staff accounts; Manager › Operations › Block Staff. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-16 Staff accounts, SCR-AUTH-10 Block Staff |
| Description | A Manager creates Staff accounts for one or more Blocks (Invited, set-password email), renames, changes the title, Blocks, what the person handles and the duty status, disables and restores; sees each Staff member's open and finished work. |
| Rules and validation | Email unique; at least one Block; changes audited. |
| Abnormal cases | A disabled account is signed out; an invitation link already used. |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-019, 020, 021, 049, 050 |

#### 3.2.8 FR-AUTH-08 Reconcile the enrolled list

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Residents › Reconciliation, before the next-Term fees (M5) and at the start of a Term. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-17 Reconciliation (enrolled list) |
| Description | The Manager uploads the enrolled list (or a leavers list) of a Term. The result groups: (1) someone of the Term not enrolled, (2) a resident missing from the list, (3) a code no student has, (4) an enrollment status that changed (directory updated). Items of groups 1–2 are resolved one by one with a note. |
| Rules and validation | BR-23: a note is required; *Not enrolled* releases the next-Term Bed, rejects an open Application, or starts a termination for a resident during the Term. Next-Term fees stay blocked while items are open (BR-22). |
| Abnormal cases | File errors as in FR-AUTH-05; resolving an item twice is refused. |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-053, 054, 055 |

#### 3.2.9 FR-AUTH-09 Audit Log

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › System › Audit Log; automatic on every audited action. |
| Actors | Administrator (read); every user (writes by acting) |
| Screens | SCR-AUTH-12 Audit Log |
| Description | Records who did what and when: configuration changes, irreversible actions (confirmations, decisions, terminations), exports, door-code views, imports, demo resets. Filters by actor, action, object and date range; labels in the user's language. |
| Rules and validation | Nobody can edit or delete entries (BR-34); the date range is checked; retention by system parameter. |
| Abnormal cases | A bad date range is refused (400). |
| Tests | TC-AUTH-014, 018 |

### 3.3 Registration periods and configuration (CFG)

#### 3.3.1 FR-CFG-01 Room Types, Room Classes and fees

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Prices and fees. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-02 Room Types, SCR-CFG-03 Room Classes, SCR-CFG-04 Deposit |
| Description | Room Types (name, number of Beds, base price per Term, roommate invitation allowed only for 2 Beds) with inventory counts; Room Classes (Basic, Standard, Premium: surcharge, amenities, where used); Deposit percentage, refund rules per trigger (percentage and approver). Defaults apply to Terms built afterwards. |
| Rules and validation | Names unique; surcharge bounded; refund rates 0–100 %; changing a Room Type's Beds adds or retires Beds in its Rooms (refused when Beds are occupied). A change of money rules creates a change announcement (BR-33). |
| Abnormal cases | Out-of-range values named per field. |
| Tests | TC-CFG-005, 006, 007, 008, 043 (TC-NTF-043) |

#### 3.3.2 FR-CFG-02 Utility prices and Utility Deposit

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Prices and fees › Utility. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-20 Utility |
| Description | Electricity and water unit prices with the month they apply from, rounding rule, due days, the Utility Deposit (estimate per month × months held). |
| Rules and validation | Values from the option lists; change audited. |
| Abnormal cases | Values outside the lists refused. |
| Tests | TC-CFG-013 |

#### 3.3.3 FR-CFG-03 Rules: who may apply, priority, matching, deadlines, stay

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Rules. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-05 Who may apply, SCR-CFG-06 Roommate matching, SCR-CFG-24 Deadlines and reminders, SCR-CFG-25 Refunds, penalties and terminations, SCR-CFG-26 Stay and renewal |
| Description | Each eligibility criterion as a sentence with on/off and "n students fail this now"; ordered priority groups with member counts; matching criteria with levels (weights) and a preview against current Applications (dry run); deadlines and reminder days; refund, termination and late check-in limits; *Gia hạn* maximum, automatic extension, share reserved for new students, escalation hours before M4. |
| Rules and validation | Weights total 100 %; saving creates the next rules snapshot (a Term keeps the snapshot of its publication); each setting shows where it acts; out-of-range values refused; changes audited and announced. |
| Abnormal cases | Saving while an assignment run is in progress uses the new snapshot only for later runs. |
| Tests | TC-CFG-009, 010, 024, 025 |

#### 3.3.4 FR-CFG-04 Registration-period requests

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Registration › Period requests › New; Admin › Registration periods › Requests. |
| Actors | Manager (files, comments), Administrator (answers) |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-22 Registration-period requests |
| Description | A Manager proposes a target Term: milestones, Blocks, Rooms left out (typed or imported from an Excel or CSV list of Room codes), places per Room Type × Room Class × gender, proposed prices, notes. Every Admin and other Manager is notified; others comment. The Admin moves it In progress, asks for changes with a note, rejects with a reason, or builds the Term from it (FR-CFG-05). |
| Rules and validation | One open request per target Term; required fields and known Blocks named per field; states Submitted → In progress → Needs changes → Done / Rejected (state diagram in Report 4). |
| Abnormal cases | A second open request for the same Term; Staff cannot file; an unknown Room code in the import is listed and left out. |
| Tests | TC-CFG-016, 017, 018, TC-INV-025 |

#### 3.3.5 FR-CFG-05 Build and publish a Term (wizard)

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Registration periods › Terms › New, or *Build the Term from this request*. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-01 Terms, SCR-CFG-23 Term wizard |
| Description | Seven steps saved as a draft: General (code, name, stay dates), Timeline (renewal milestones M1–M7 and registration milestones on a visual timeline), Rooms and places (Blocks, Rooms left out, Room Class per Room for the Term, supply and demand), Prices (per Room Type × Room Class, Deposit %, Utility Deposit), Rules (snapshot), Information (house rules, FAQ, documents), Review and publish. Publishing fixes prices and rules, creates the Term announcement and notifies students and Managers. |
| Rules and validation | Order of milestones M1 ≤ M2 < M3 < M4 ≤ M5 ≤ M6 < M7 < stay end, registration close ≤ results, check-in start ≥ previous Term's check-out (per-field messages); a Draft is invisible to students; a Draft with unsaved steps cannot be published; after publishing, passed dates are fixed and open deadlines can only be extended, with a reason and a change announcement (BR-09). |
| Abnormal cases | Values changed from the Manager's request need a reason; publishing twice is refused. |
| Tests | TC-CFG-001–004, 019–023 |

#### 3.3.6 FR-CFG-06 Block settings

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Operations › Block Settings. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-20 Block Settings |
| Description | Desk hours, visiting and quiet hours, house rules and time limits of a Block within the Admin's limits. A change becomes an announcement to the Block's residents. |
| Rules and validation | Values inside the Admin limits and in order (opening before closing); Manager only; audited. |
| Abnormal cases | Out-of-limit values named per field. |
| Tests | TC-CFG-014, 015, TC-NTF-043 |

#### 3.3.7 FR-CFG-07 System parameters

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › System › System Parameters. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-08 System Parameters |
| Description | Typed parameters (numbers, hours, switches) used by the rules and jobs, e.g. `stay.max_terms`, `payment.rejected_claim_min_hours`, `late_check_in.max_days`, `sla.unassigned_max_hours`. |
| Rules and validation | Value checked against its type and range; an invalid value is named by its key. |
| Abnormal cases | Manager or Staff: 403. |
| Tests | TC-CFG-011, 012 |

#### 3.3.8 FR-CFG-08 Demo data reset

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › System › Demo data (only when the server runs with `DEMO_TOOLS=true`). |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-27 Demo data |
| Description | Lists the stages (0 base data, A registration, B residence, C Term transition), the scenario accounts and sample files; a reset replaces business data with the stage's scenarios dated relative to today, keeps accounts and Blocks and is audited. |
| Rules and validation | Known stage and `RESET` typed to confirm; refused without the base data; off unless the server enables it. |
| Abnormal cases | Unknown sample file: 404; tools off: refused. |
| Tests | TC-CFG-026–029 |

### 3.4 Inventory, Room Classes, furniture and door codes (INV)

#### 3.4.1 FR-INV-01 Blocks, Floors, Rooms and Beds

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Buildings and rooms; Staff and Manager › Rooms. |
| Actors | Administrator (structure), Staff and Manager (view, out of service) |
| Screens | SCR-INV-01 Buildings and Structure, SCR-INV-10 Room and Bed Inventory |
| Description | Blocks with gender, Floors and Rooms; bulk generation of Rooms of a Floor with a Room Type and Room Class; the room map with each Bed's state (empty, assigned unpaid, resident, leaving, moving in next Term, out of service) for the current or next Term; a Room out of service and back with a reason. |
| Rules and validation | Generating again adds nothing; bad ranges refused; an occupied Room cannot go out of service, its Block cannot change gender; Staff see only their Blocks. |
| Abnormal cases | Unknown Room: 404; a student cannot read the inventory. |
| Tests | TC-INV-001–007, 012 |

#### 3.4.2 FR-INV-02 Room Classes by Term

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Inventory › Room Classes by Term; Term wizard step 3. |
| Actors | Manager, Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-INV-11 Room Classes by Term |
| Description | Sets the Room Class of Rooms from a Term on; shows each Room's class and furniture conformance for the next Term to start. |
| Rules and validation | BR-11: only before the Term starts and when none of the Room's Beds is given for that Term; earlier Terms keep their class; Manager only. |
| Abnormal cases | A running Term or a Room with an Allocation keeps its class (refused with the reason). |
| Tests | TC-INV-008–011 |

#### 3.4.3 FR-INV-03 Furniture

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Buildings and rooms › Furniture types; Staff and Manager › Rooms › Furniture. |
| Actors | Administrator (types, Room Class requirements), Manager (register items, transfers between Blocks), Staff (moves in the Block, status) |
| Screens | SCR-INV-14 Furniture types, SCR-INV-13 Furniture, My Room (furniture list) |
| Description | Furniture types (VI/EN names, category, defines Room Class or standard) and the types and quantities each Room Class requires; items with an asset code (printable QR label), status (In use, Broken, In repair, In store, Disposed) and place (a Room or a Block store); moves with reason and history; conformance of each Room to its Room Class. |
| Rules and validation | Codes fixed after creation; status follows the place; Disposed is final; Staff move only inside their Blocks; every move recorded. |
| Abnormal cases | Inactive type in a requirement; an item of another Block. |
| Tests | TC-INV-013–018 |

#### 3.4.4 FR-INV-04 Door codes

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Staff › Rooms › Door codes; a "change door code" task; My Room › Show the door code. |
| Actors | Staff (set, import, confirm), Student and Staff (view) |
| Screens | SCR-INV-12 Door codes, SCR-ASG-01 My Room |
| Description | Each Room has one current 6-digit code. Staff draw a random code (never the previous one), type one, or import a CSV (Room, code); they set it on the lock and confirm it, and it becomes Active, retiring the old one. When a resident leaves a Room, a task asks the Block's Staff for a new code. Students whose Balance is paid see the code from the check-in start, behind a *Show* button. |
| Rules and validation | BR-14, BR-15: codes encrypted at rest, never in push or email text, every view audited; CSV checked line by line before anything is proposed. |
| Abnormal cases | Other Blocks or roles refused; a student before release sees "waiting for the code". |
| Tests | TC-INV-019–023 |

#### 3.4.5 FR-INV-05 Room hub

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | A Room code in any list or in the header search. |
| Actors | Staff, Manager, Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-INV-14 Room hub |
| Description | One page per Room: residents of the current and next Term, Room Class per Term and furniture conformance, door code status, meter readings, Maintenance Requests and inspections. |
| Rules and validation | Block scope (BR-32). |
| Abnormal cases | A Room outside the Staff's Blocks: 404. |
| Tests | TC-INV-024 |

### 3.5 Applications (APP)

#### 3.5.1 FR-APP-01 Eligibility and the open Term

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student Home › Apply; the registration period card. |
| Actors | Student |
| Screens | SCR-HOME-05 Registration period details, SCR-APP-01 Application Wizard – 1 Term and eligibility |
| Description | Shows the Term open for registration (timeline, prices, Rooms, house rules, FAQ) and checks every enabled eligibility criterion for the student, each with a pass or fail sentence. |
| Rules and validation | BR-02: verified account, enrolled, not a continuing resident of the Term, no overdue Invoice, plus the Admin's criteria. |
| Abnormal cases | No open Term: the card says when the next opens; a failed check explains why and stops the wizard. |
| Tests | TC-APP-001, 022, TC-CFG-023 |

#### 3.5.2 FR-APP-02 Apply and receive the Deposit Invoice

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Application Wizard steps 2–4. |
| Actors | Student |
| Screens | SCR-APP-01 Application Wizard (Room preference, Roommate, Personal info, Review and submit) |
| Description | The student chooses Room Type and Room Class (with the Term price), the roommate mode, *Gia hạn* (Terms committed), confirms contact details and accepts the house rules and consent, then submits. The Application is Awaiting Deposit and a Deposit Invoice is issued; Home and a notification show the next step. |
| Rules and validation | BR-01, BR-03, BR-05, BR-06: one open Application per Term; contact, consent and roommate fields named per field; *Gia hạn* from 1 to `stay.max_terms`, capped by semesters left. |
| Abnormal cases | A second Application for the Term: 409; registration closed: refused. |
| Tests | TC-APP-002, 003, 023 |

#### 3.5.3 FR-APP-03 Roommate invitation (2-bed Rooms)

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Roommate step of the wizard; the invitation notification. |
| Actors | Student (inviter and invitee) |
| Screens | SCR-APP-01 Roommate (2-bed), SCR-APP-04 Roommate Invitation |
| Description | The inviter types the partner's student code; the partner accepts or declines within the roommate window. Each pays their own Deposit; the first to pay waits as Awaiting Roommate until the other's Deposit is confirmed, then both are Submitted together. |
| Rules and validation | BR-04: only 2-bed Room Types; the same answer for every unusable code and a limited number of checks (privacy). |
| Abnormal cases | A declined or expired invitation leaves the inviter matched automatically. |
| Tests | TC-APP-004, 005, 006, TC-ASG-001, 003 |

#### 3.5.4 FR-APP-04 Cancel or expire an Application

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | My Applications › Cancel; the Deposit expiry job. |
| Actors | Student, System |
| Screens | SCR-APP-02 My Applications, SCR-APP-03 Application Detail |
| Description | Before the assignment the student cancels; an unpaid Deposit Invoice is voided, a paid one is refunded by the refund rule. An Application whose Deposit window ends without a claim expires and its Invoice is voided. The student may apply again while registration is open. |
| Rules and validation | BR-07, BR-28. |
| Abnormal cases | Cancelling after the assignment follows the *Cancel after results* refund rule. |
| Tests | TC-APP-007, 008 |

#### 3.5.5 FR-APP-05 Review Applications

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Registration › Applications. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-APP-10 Application Queue, SCR-APP-11 Application Review |
| Description | The queue of Submitted Applications with filters; opening one starts the review (Under Review); the Manager approves or rejects, one by one or in bulk with a confirmation of the count. |
| Rules and validation | Rejection needs a note; a decision is made once; every Manager sees every Block (ADR-19). |
| Abnormal cases | Staff and students: 403; a decided Application: 409. |
| Tests | TC-APP-010, 011, TC-ASG-010 |

#### 3.5.6 FR-APP-06 My Applications and history

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student › Registration › My Applications. |
| Actors | Student |
| Screens | SCR-APP-02 My Applications, SCR-APP-03 Application Detail |
| Description | The student's Applications of every Term with status, Room preference, *Gia hạn*, Invoices and the timeline of events. |
| Rules and validation | Own data only. |
| Abnormal cases | Another student's Application: 404. |
| Tests | TC-APP-002, 009 |

#### 3.5.7 FR-APP-07 Round 2 offers

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Registration › Round 2; the offer notification. |
| Actors | Manager, Student |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-02 Round 2 Offer |
| Description | Waitlisted students are offered held Beds freed by forfeits, unpaid next-Term fees, ended stays and terminations. A student accepts one option (Allocated, Balance Invoice issued) or declines; offers expire. |
| Rules and validation | Options match the student's gender and preference; one acceptance per student. |
| Abnormal cases | An expired offer cannot be accepted. |
| Tests | TC-APP-020, TC-APP-021 |

### 3.6 Assignment, residence and Term transition (ASG)

#### 3.6.1 FR-ASG-01 Run the assignment

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Registration › Assignment › Run. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-10 Assignment Runs |
| Description | The engine places Approved Applications: hard constraints first (Block gender, Room Type and Room Class applied for, invited pairs together, capacity), then priority groups, then the matching criteria and weights of the Term's snapshot. A dry run is a preview that allocates nothing; a real run creates a proposal. |
| Rules and validation | BR-12, BR-13: deterministic (the same input gives the same proposal); a real run only after M3 and with no next-Term request open. |
| Abnormal cases | A student no longer eligible is flagged and never placed; students and Staff: 403. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-001–006, 011 |

#### 3.6.2 FR-ASG-02 Review conflicts

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Opening a run's proposal. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-11 Assignment Proposal Review |
| Description | Lists placements per Block and conflicts: NO_BED (nothing left), PARTNER_NOT_READY (invited partner not in the run), LOW_FIT (information). The Manager resolves each conflict (another Bed, waitlist). |
| Rules and validation | Conflicts are never resolved silently. |
| Abnormal cases | A Block with an open conflict cannot be committed. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-003, 006, 010 |

#### 3.6.3 FR-ASG-03 Commit the assignment

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | *Commit* per Block or for all Blocks. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-11 Assignment Proposal Review |
| Description | Committing creates Allocations (Assigned – unpaid) and Balance Invoices (Term price − Deposit + Utility Deposit), marks the others Waitlisted, starts the Stay and notifies each student. |
| Rules and validation | BR-08, NFR-03: one Allocation per Bed per Term and per student per Term (database rule). |
| Abnormal cases | A Bed taken meanwhile: refused, run again. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-010, 020 |

#### 3.6.4 FR-ASG-04 Door code release, check-in and My Room

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | The release job; the Check-in Desk; Student › My Room. |
| Actors | System, Staff, Student |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-11 Check-in Desk, SCR-ASG-01 My Room |
| Description | When the Balance is paid, the check-in start has come and the Room's code is confirmed, the student receives the door code and becomes a resident. At the desk Staff find the student by code, name or the check-in pass (QR) and record the hand-over (key, card, items). My Room shows the Room, Bed, roommates, furniture, door code, Stay and next-Term status. |
| Rules and validation | BR-14: unpaid Balance blocks check-in at the desk; Staff only for their Blocks; every Manager can use the desk. |
| Abnormal cases | Another Block's Staff do not find the student; students and the Admin have no desk. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-020, 021, 032, TC-INV-023 |

#### 3.6.5 FR-ASG-05 Late check-in

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student › Requests › Late check-in; Staff at the desk; Manager › Decisions. |
| Actors | Student, Staff, Manager |
| Screens | SCR-MNT-01 My Requests, SCR-REQ-11 Check-in Desk, SCR-REQ-20 Decisions |
| Description | The student (online) or Staff (at the desk) record a request with reason, day and evidence file. A Manager approves with a new deadline or rejects with a reason. An approved one extends the Balance deadline and the arrival deadline. |
| Rules and validation | BR-16: asked before the check-in end plus `late_check_in.max_days`; a rejection needs a reason. |
| Abnormal cases | Too late a day: field message; a decided request cannot be decided again. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-030, 031, 037 |

#### 3.6.6 FR-ASG-06 Check-out and settlement

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Staff › Desk › Check-out. |
| Actors | Staff, Manager (refund) |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-12 Check-out Desk |
| Description | Staff record the final meter reading, key or card returned, the Room's condition and the damage of each furniture item. The Utility Deposit is settled: the student's Utility share since the last reading and the damage are deducted, the rest goes to a refund for a Manager, a shortfall becomes an Invoice. The Allocation ends and a door-code task opens. |
| Rules and validation | BR-24, BR-15. |
| Abnormal cases | Charges above the Utility Deposit: the rest invoiced; a leaver who has not checked out by the date appears on the overdue check-out list. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-022, 023, 045, TC-BIL-029 |

#### 3.6.7 FR-ASG-07 Open and close the requests window

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Scheduled job at M2 and M3 of the next Term. |
| Actors | System |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-20 Term transition, SCR-ASG-01 My Room (next-Term status) |
| Description | At M2 every resident not leaving gets a next-Term Allocation on the same Bed: Continuing (Terms left in the Stay) or Awaiting extension (last Term), and students are told. At M3 filing closes and Beds still Awaiting extension are released (the student is told in-app and by email). |
| Rules and validation | BR-17: runs once per Term; the database holds one next-Term Allocation per Bed. |
| Abnormal cases | A terminated resident gets no next-Term Allocation. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-038, 039 |

#### 3.6.8 FR-ASG-08 Issue next-Term fees and the M7 deadline

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Finance › Next-Term fees (M6); job at M7. |
| Actors | Manager, System |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-20 Term transition |
| Description | A preview shows count and total per Block, Room Type and Room Class and what blocks issuing; issuing gives each continuing resident one Invoice "Room fee · Term N+1 · Room X" = 100 % of the next Term's price. At M7 an unpaid fee with no claim waiting is voided and its Bed released (nothing kept); a paid one makes the student a resident of the new Term at the turnover. |
| Rules and validation | BR-22: filing closed, every request decided, reconciliation resolved. |
| Abnormal cases | Blockers listed by name; issuing twice is refused. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-040, 041, 042 |

#### 3.6.9 FR-ASG-09 Terminations

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Residents › Terminations › New; Utility debt rule; reconciliation (*Not enrolled*). |
| Actors | Manager, System |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-12 Terminations |
| Description | A termination has a reason and a move-out date: Notice sent → Checked out (desk), Cancelled (Manager, with a reason) or Overdue (date passed: Managers and the Block's Staff told, door code rotated). At move-out the Allocation and next-Term Allocation end and refunds follow the rule. |
| Rules and validation | BR-26, BR-27, BR-28. |
| Abnormal cases | Cancelling after check-out is refused. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-035, 036, TC-BIL-038 |

#### 3.6.10 FR-ASG-10 Operational moves and turnover

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Staff or Manager › Operational moves; the turnover week. |
| Actors | Staff (own Blocks), Manager |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-21 Operational moves, SCR-ASG-20 Term transition, SCR-HOME-02 Staff Dashboard |
| Description | Moves a resident to another Bed for a recorded reason (Room unusable, safety, conflict, other) without charge: both meters are read, the old Room's code must change, the new Room's code is released; the next-Term Allocation follows. The turnover lists leavers to check out, movers, arriving students, Rooms needing a reading and a new code. |
| Rules and validation | BR-18: no price difference; after next-Term fees are issued Staff can no longer move a next-Term Bed (a Manager can move an unpaid one). |
| Abnormal cases | Target Bed taken or of the wrong gender: refused. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-042, 043, 044 |

#### 3.6.11 FR-ASG-11 Balance deadline and forfeit

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Scheduled job every 5 minutes; reminders before the deadline. |
| Actors | System |
| Screens | SCR-BIL-01 My Invoices (deadline), notifications |
| Description | Reminders 3 and 1 days before the Balance deadline. A Balance past its deadline with no claim waiting and no approved late check-in is forfeited: Allocation cancelled, Balance void, Application Forfeited, Deposit kept by the *Balance not paid* rule, Bed to Round 2. |
| Rules and validation | BR-07, BR-08. |
| Abnormal cases | Two rejected claims cancel the Balance with its Allocation. |
| Tests | TC-ASG-033, 034, TC-BIL-036 |

### 3.7 Payments and billing (BIL)

#### 3.7.1 FR-BIL-01 Invoices and the VietQR payment page

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student › Payments; a link from Home or a notification. |
| Actors | Student (own Invoices), Manager and Admin (all) |
| Screens | SCR-BIL-01 My Invoices, SCR-BIL-02 Invoice Payment, SCR-BIL-03 Utility Invoice; SCR-BIL-10 Payments |
| Description | Lists Invoices (Deposit, Balance, next-Term fee, Utility, charges) with status and deadline. The payment page shows the VietQR image (bank, account, amount, transfer content), the amount and the deadline; the QR can be refreshed. |
| Rules and validation | Amounts fixed once issued; transfer content unique per Invoice. |
| Abnormal cases | Another student's Invoice: 404; bank account not configured: the page shows the details without the image. |
| Tests | TC-BIL-001, 006, 010 |

#### 3.7.2 FR-BIL-02 Claim a transfer

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | *I have transferred* on the payment page. |
| Actors | Student |
| Screens | SCR-BIL-02 Invoice Payment |
| Description | The student enters the bank reference (and optionally a receipt). The Invoice becomes Awaiting confirmation and every deadline that depends on it stops. |
| Rules and validation | BR-07: one claim at a time; a paid or void Invoice and a Deposit past its deadline cannot be claimed; a next-Term fee cannot be claimed while a Utility Invoice is overdue; a Utility Invoice claimed after its due date stays overdue. |
| Abnormal cases | Claim on someone else's Invoice: 404. |
| Tests | TC-BIL-032, 034, 035 |

#### 3.7.3 FR-BIL-03 Confirm or reject claims

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Finance › Payment confirmations; the hourly summary notification. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-BIL-13 Payment confirmations |
| Description | The queue of claims with filters (type, Term, Block, claimed since); the Manager selects one or many and confirms (dialog with count and total) or rejects with a reason. Confirming marks the Invoice Paid and runs the next step (Application Submitted, door code release, next-Term residence). A Manager can also confirm an Invoice that was not claimed, with the bank reference and a receipt. |
| Rules and validation | Each Invoice confirmed and audited separately; a rejection gives back the time left (at least `payment.rejected_claim_min_hours`); a second rejection cancels a Deposit or Balance; receipt files are type-checked. |
| Abnormal cases | A void Invoice cannot be confirmed; Staff: 403. |
| Tests | TC-BIL-011, 012, 032, 033 |

#### 3.7.4 FR-BIL-04 Meter readings and Utility Invoices

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Staff › Utility › Meter Readings (monthly). |
| Actors | Staff |
| Screens | SCR-UTL-10 Meter Readings |
| Description | The month's period opens on first use; Staff enter or import (CSV) electricity and water readings of each occupied Room and close the month. Closing issues each resident's Utility Invoice with its breakdown; the share follows the days each resident lived in the Room between meter cuts (check-out, move). |
| Rules and validation | BR-25: a reading may not go back; an unusual jump needs a confirmation; a CSV is checked line by line before anything is saved; a closed month is read-only; totals round up. |
| Abnormal cases | A Room without a reading at the end has nothing to share yet. |
| Tests | TC-BIL-022–026, 029, 030, 031 |

#### 3.7.5 FR-BIL-05 Overdue Invoices and Utility debt

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Hourly job; Manager › Finance › Overdue and reminders. |
| Actors | System, Manager |
| Screens | SCR-BIL-20 Block Finance |
| Description | An unpaid charge past its due date becomes Overdue and the student is told. Utility debt: one overdue month gives warning 1 (in-app and email), a second overdue month or debt reaching the Utility Deposit gives the final warning with a termination day, and from that day the stay is terminated (FR-ASG-09). Paying closes the warnings. |
| Rules and validation | BR-26: each warning once; a Balance past its deadline is forfeited, not overdue. |
| Abnormal cases | A claim waiting holds the warning. |
| Tests | TC-BIL-020, 037, 038 |

#### 3.7.6 FR-BIL-06 Refunds

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Cancellation, check-out settlement, termination; Manager › Finance › Refunds. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-20 Decisions (refunds), SCR-BIL-20 Block Finance |
| Description | A refund is created by its trigger with the rule's percentage and waits for its approver; the Manager approves (the Invoice becomes Refunded) or rejects with a note; the student is told. |
| Rules and validation | BR-28: at most one refund per Invoice. |
| Abnormal cases | Rejection without a note refused. |
| Tests | TC-BIL-021, TC-APP-007 |

#### 3.7.7 FR-BIL-07 Payment reminders and collections

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Hourly job; Manager › Finance. |
| Actors | System, Manager |
| Screens | SCR-BIL-10 Payments, SCR-BIL-20 Block Finance, SCR-HOME-03 Manager Dashboard |
| Description | Reminders before the Balance and next-Term fee deadlines (days set by the Admin), once each and never while a claim waits; one hourly summary of waiting claims to Managers; collections per Block with CSV export. |
| Rules and validation | Reminder days from configuration. |
| Abnormal cases | — |
| Tests | TC-BIL-036, TC-RPT-006 |

### 3.8 Requests and time limits (REQ)

#### 3.8.1 FR-REQ-01 Next-Term room change

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student › Requests › Room change (between M2 and M3). |
| Actors | Student, Staff, Manager |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-02 New Room-Change Request, SCR-REQ-10 Room-Change Queue |
| Description | The student sees the next-Term Bed and the next Term's prices and asks for another Room Type, Room Class or Block with a reason. Staff of the Block (or a Manager across Blocks) approve with a free matching Bed of the next Term, chosen by them, and the next-Term Allocation moves there; or reject with a listed reason. |
| Rules and validation | BR-18: one open request per student; students never pick the Bed; due at M4. |
| Abnormal cases | No matching Bed: rejected with that reason; students cannot decide. |
| Tests | TC-REQ-001, 002, 003, 015 |

#### 3.8.2 FR-REQ-02 Swap next-Term Beds

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student › Requests › Swap (a specific student or the swap board). |
| Actors | Students (both), Staff, Manager |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-03 Room Swap, SCR-REQ-04 Swap Board, SCR-REQ-05 Swap Invitation, SCR-REQ-13 Room Swap Requests |
| Description | A direct swap: the partner accepts, Staff check and approve, the two next-Term Allocations exchange Beds. The swap board shows anonymous posts of next-Term Beds with their next-Term price; a matching request becomes a swap. |
| Rules and validation | BR-20: across Blocks Staff then a Manager decide; an unanswered swap expires; after next-Term fees are issued no swap is carried out. |
| Abnormal cases | Partner declines; a post no longer available. |
| Tests | TC-REQ-010, 011, 012 |

#### 3.8.3 FR-REQ-03 Room Class change of a Room

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student › Requests › Room Class change; the consent notification. |
| Actors | Students of the Room, Staff |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-08 Room Class change, SCR-REQ-10 Room-Change Queue |
| Description | A continuing resident asks for another Room Class from the next Term; every other continuing resident must agree; Staff check the furniture (items to reserve or remove) and approve; the Room's class for the next Term changes and furniture move tasks are created. |
| Rules and validation | BR-19: a resident in the last Term of the Stay is not asked; a decline ends the request. |
| Abnormal cases | Missing furniture in the stores: rejected. |
| Tests | TC-REQ-020 |

#### 3.8.4 FR-REQ-04 Extend the stay or end it

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student › My Room › Stay. |
| Actors | Student, Staff |
| Screens | SCR-ASG-01 My Room, SCR-MNT-01 My Requests |
| Description | An extension (+k Terms) in the Stay's last Term is approved at once when the student is enrolled and has nothing overdue (the Bed is kept, the Stay commits more Terms); otherwise Staff decide. Ending the stay after this Term cancels the next-Term Allocation and frees the Bed. |
| Rules and validation | BR-05, BR-21. |
| Abnormal cases | After M3: filing closed. |
| Tests | TC-REQ-019 |

#### 3.8.5 FR-REQ-05 Decide next-Term requests

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Staff › Requests; Manager › Residents › Requests across Blocks. |
| Actors | Staff (own Blocks), Manager |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-10 Room-Change Queue, SCR-REQ-13 Room Swap Requests, SCR-REQ-20 Decisions |
| Description | One list of room changes, swaps, Room Class changes and extensions, oldest first, with time left to M4; bulk decisions with a confirmation of the count. |
| Rules and validation | Every request decided by M4; undecided ones escalate 48 hours before (FR-REQ-07). |
| Abnormal cases | A request of another Block: 404 for Staff. |
| Tests | TC-REQ-021, 018 |

#### 3.8.6 FR-REQ-06 Routing rules and time limits

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Operations › Request Routing Rules. |
| Actors | Manager |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-20 Request Routing Rules, SCR-AUTH-10 Block Staff |
| Description | Rules per Block choose the assignee of a new request by type and category (a category rule first, else the rule for all), with a fallback when the assignee is off duty; the Block's urgent and normal time limits; the staff list with open and finished work. |
| Rules and validation | BR-29; Manager only, in scope. |
| Abnormal cases | Gaps (no rule for a category) are shown. |
| Tests | TC-REQ-013, 014, 015, 022 |

#### 3.8.7 FR-REQ-07 Overdue requests (escalations)

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Scan every 15 minutes; Manager › Operations › Overdue requests. |
| Actors | System, Manager |
| Screens | SCR-REQ-21 Escalations, SCR-HOME-03 Manager Dashboard |
| Description | A request past its deadline, or unassigned longer than `sla.unassigned_max_hours`, opens one escalation for Managers; the Manager reassigns it or notes the action (an undecided room change may get a temporary Bed); it closes by itself once the request is back on track. |
| Rules and validation | BR-30: one open escalation per request. |
| Abnormal cases | Staff cannot act on escalations. |
| Tests | TC-REQ-016, 017, 018 |

### 3.9 Maintenance and inspections (MNT)

#### 3.9.1 FR-MNT-01 Report a Maintenance Request

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Student › Requests › New Maintenance Request; Staff on behalf of a Room. |
| Actors | Student (resident), Staff |
| Screens | SCR-MNT-02 New Maintenance Request, SCR-MNT-01 My Requests |
| Description | Category, location, urgency, description, photos and optionally the furniture item; the request is routed (FR-REQ-06) and gets its deadline from the Block's time limit. The student follows its status and updates. |
| Rules and validation | Only a resident of the Room; photos are images within the size limit; fields named per field. |
| Abnormal cases | A student without a Room: refused. |
| Tests | TC-MNT-001, 008, TC-REQ-014 |

#### 3.9.2 FR-MNT-02 Handle Maintenance Requests

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Staff › Maintenance › Queue. |
| Actors | Staff (own Blocks), Manager |
| Screens | SCR-MNT-10 Maintenance Queue, SCR-MNT-11 Maintenance Detail |
| Description | Assign, plan the visit, post updates, mark resolved; the student is told, confirms (Closed) or reopens once; Staff may close a duplicate. The item's repair history is kept. |
| Rules and validation | Block scope; time left shown in green, amber, red. |
| Abnormal cases | Another Block's Staff neither see nor count the request. |
| Tests | TC-MNT-002, 003 |

#### 3.9.3 FR-MNT-03 Inspection checklists

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Rules › Inspection Checklists. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-21 Inspection Checklists |
| Description | Checklists with items; a Draft is published as v1, editing publishes v2 and keeps v1 as Replaced; archiving pauses the schedules that use it. Rooms' own checks (number of people matches the residents, furniture items) are added to every run. |
| Rules and validation | A schedule cannot resume until another checklist is published. |
| Abnormal cases | — |
| Tests | TC-MNT-004, 006 |

#### 3.9.4 FR-MNT-04 Inspection schedules and runs

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Operations › Inspection Schedule; the daily job at 06:00. |
| Actors | Manager (schedules), Staff (runs) |
| Screens | SCR-MNT-20 Inspection Schedule, SCR-MNT-12 Inspection Checklist |
| Description | A recurring schedule per Block starts its runs (the first at once) and notifies residents; Staff record each Room's answers and its own checks; a failed item creates a Maintenance Request. |
| Rules and validation | BR-31; schedules are the Managers', runs need Staff. |
| Abnormal cases | A Room's run is not done until its own checks are answered. |
| Tests | TC-MNT-005, 007 |

### 3.10 Notifications and announcements (NTF)

#### 3.10.1 FR-NTF-01 In-app notifications

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Every business event of the table in Change Specification §10; the bell. |
| Actors | All signed-in users |
| Screens | Bell panel (web), MOB-NTF-01 Notifications (phone) |
| Description | Newest first with the unread count; mark one or all read; a notification links to its object. Title and body are stored in both languages and shown in the reader's language. |
| Rules and validation | Own notifications only. |
| Abnormal cases | Someone else's notification: 404; not signed in: 401. |
| Tests | TC-NTF-001, 002, 003, 038 |

#### 3.10.2 FR-NTF-02 Push and email delivery

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | After the transaction of an event commits. |
| Actors | System |
| Screens | — (Android notification tray, mailbox) |
| Description | Push messages through Firebase Cloud Messaging to the user's registered Android devices; emails queued and sent every 30 seconds by SMTP in the recipient's language. On the demo server, emails to fictional accounts go to the demo mailbox with the recipient in the subject; real accounts receive their own. |
| Rules and validation | Device tokens stored hashed; an unregistered token is disabled; no door code in any text. |
| Abnormal cases | Without SMTP nothing is sent and nothing fails; FCM errors other than an unregistered token are retried as failures. |
| Tests | TC-NTF-010, 011, 012, 020, 021, 034, 035, 039, 040 |

#### 3.10.3 FR-NTF-03 Announcements and the dormitory board

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Staff, Manager or Admin › Announcements; automatic for Term publication and rule changes. |
| Actors | Administrator, Manager (any audience), Staff (residents of their Blocks), Student (reads) |
| Screens | SCR-NTF-22 Announcements, SCR-HOME-01 Student Home (board) |
| Description | Title, body, category, audience (all students, residents, residents of Blocks, applicants of a Term), pinned, shown from / until, link. Students read them at the top of Home and in the bell; one record with a read state per user. |
| Rules and validation | BR-33. |
| Abnormal cases | Staff writing to everybody or another Block: refused. |
| Tests | TC-NTF-041, 042, 043 |

#### 3.10.4 FR-NTF-04 Notification templates

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Notifications › Templates. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-CFG-07 Notification Templates |
| Description | Each event's title and body in Vietnamese and English with variables and sample values; channels (in-app, push, email); a test sends the unsaved text to the signed-in Admin. |
| Rules and validation | Push length limit; unknown variables refused. |
| Abnormal cases | — |
| Tests | TC-NTF-030, 031, 036, 037 |

#### 3.10.5 FR-NTF-05 Send emails to student groups

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Admin › Notifications › Send Email. |
| Actors | Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-NTF-21 Send Email |
| Description | Choose a group (e.g. residents of a Block, applicants of a Term), write subject and body, preview the count and the first email, send: one email per student plus the in-app notice and push. |
| Rules and validation | System emails are not offered; fields validated; Admin only. |
| Abnormal cases | An empty group cannot be sent. |
| Tests | TC-NTF-032, 033 |

### 3.11 Dashboards, reports and search (RPT)

#### 3.11.1 FR-RPT-01 Dashboards per role

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Signing in to the back office. |
| Actors | Staff, Manager, Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-HOME-02 Staff Dashboard, SCR-HOME-03 Manager Dashboard, SCR-HOME-04 Admin Dashboard |
| Description | Staff: today's desk, review queue, Rooms out of service, Beds of the Block, what needs attention. Manager: occupancy by Block and Floor, SLA rate and target, waiting claims, approvals, overdue requests. Admin: the Term, people, the funnel, Blocks, configuration checks and integrations. |
| Rules and validation | Figures follow the user's scope; empty figures before the first Term. |
| Abnormal cases | Staff cannot read the Manager's approval counts. |
| Tests | TC-RPT-001–004, 011 |

#### 3.11.2 FR-RPT-02 Term dashboard and reports

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | Manager › Registration › Term dashboard; Reports menu. |
| Actors | Manager, Administrator |
| Screens | SCR-RPT-11 Term dashboard, SCR-RPT-01 Occupancy Report, SCR-RPT-02 Financial Report, SCR-RPT-10 Block Reports |
| Description | Term dashboard: milestones in order with progress, Applications by status, places filled per Room Type × Room Class, Deposits and Balances paid, the requests window (open requests, continuing residents, next-Term fees issued and paid). Occupancy by Block, Room Type and Room Class; money per Block; check-ins per week and who has not checked in. |
| Rules and validation | Capacity leaves Rooms out of service out; an ended Term still reports who lived there. |
| Abnormal cases | — |
| Tests | TC-RPT-005, 006, 007, 010, 012, 014 |

#### 3.11.3 FR-RPT-03 CSV export

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | *Export CSV* on any list. |
| Actors | Staff (own Blocks), Manager, Administrator |
| Screens | Every list screen |
| Description | Downloads the list with the screen's columns and filters as CSV (UTF-8 with byte-order mark for Excel); the export is written to the Audit Log. |
| Rules and validation | Correct quoting, empty cells, campus time zone; text a spreadsheet would run as a formula is neutralised. |
| Abnormal cases | Scope and permissions as the list. |
| Tests | TC-RPT-008, 009 |

#### 3.11.4 FR-RPT-04 Search and hubs

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | The search box in the back-office header. |
| Actors | Staff, Manager, Administrator |
| Screens | Header search, SCR-AUTH-14 Student hub, SCR-INV-14 Room hub |
| Description | Finds students by code or name, Rooms with or without the dash, Invoices and request codes inside the user's Blocks; opens the student hub (profile, account, Bed, Applications, Invoices, requests, history) or the Room hub. |
| Rules and validation | Block scope. |
| Abnormal cases | No result: "No results". |
| Tests | TC-RPT-013, TC-AUTH-043 |

### 3.12 Android app for students (MOB)

#### 3.12.1 FR-MOB-01 Student app

| Item | Description |
|---|---|
| Trigger | The student installs the app (APK of the release) and signs in. |
| Actors | Student |
| Screens | Android: Sign in, Home, My Room, Payments, Activity (requests and notifications) |
| Description | The student portal on the phone with the same API: Home with the board and the next step, My Room (Room, roommates, door code, check-in pass, furniture), Invoices with the VietQR page and the claim, Maintenance Requests with photos, notifications with push. The device token is registered for push after sign-in and removed at sign-out. |
| Rules and validation | Same rules as the web portal (the API enforces them); Vietnamese or English from the phone's language. |
| Abnormal cases | No network: a retry message; an expired session returns to sign-in. |
| Tests | Manual (Report 5, section 2.3); push delivery TC-NTF-020, 021 |
